.TH GFXHAT 1
.SH NAME
gfxhat \- the console's log on a Pimoroni GFX HAT
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B gfxhat
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B gfxhat
shows what a serial wire would show on a Raspberry Pi 4's GFX HAT: its
128 x 64 screen holds 8 lines of 21 characters; long lines wrap. It
follows the log as it grows; the touch buttons go back in it:
.TP
.BR up ", " down
a line;
.TP
.BR minus ", " plus
a page;
.TP
.B back
the newest;
.TP
.B select
the contrast on the last row (minus and plus change it; back, or 4 s
untouched, keeps it); select again: the backlight off or on.
.PP
Scrolled back, a bar on the right says where. It is started by
.BR init (8)
as background work; with no Raspberry Pi GPIO or no HAT it ends with 0
at once and is not started again.
.SH FILES
.TP
.B /etc/gfxhat.conf
the contrast chosen.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR dmesg (1),
.BR gpio (1)
